<&_ if (fragment.testingSection) { -&>
#### E2E tests

UI end-to-end tests are powered by [Playwright](https://playwright.dev/). They're located in [<%= playwrightDir %>](<%= playwrightDir %>)
and can be run by starting Spring Boot in one terminal (`<%= nodePackageManagerCommand %> run app:start`) and running the tests (`<%= nodePackageManagerCommand %> run e2e`) in a second one.

Before running Playwright tests, it's possible to specify user or admin credentials by overriding the `LOGIN_USER` and `PASSWORD_USER` environment variables or the `LOGIN_ADMIN` and `PASSWORD_ADMIN` environment variables.

```
export LOGIN_USER="<your-username>"
export PASSWORD_USER="<your-password>"
export LOGIN_ADMIN="<your-username>"
export PASSWORD_ADMIN="<your-password>"
```

It is also possible to use different environment file, the default one is located at [<%= playwrightDir %>/.env](<%= playwrightDir %>/.env).
[Dotenvx](https://dotenvx.com/) is used for reading environment files, it can also be used to encrypt sensible data like password.
See Dotenvx documentation for setting OS environment variables to learn more.

<&_ } -&>
